{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>Of the sons of Joseph: of the sons of Ephraim</b> – He placed Ephraim before Manasseh and traced Joseph's genealogy upon him, and likewise below in the arrangement of the banners (Numbers 2:18–20), for he was the banner-leader and he is the firstborn while his brother is secondary, according to Jacob's blessing (Genesis 48:20). And furthermore, because the sons of Ephraim were more numerous than the sons of Manasseh. But in the second census, in the plains of Moab, he placed Manasseh first, for at that time the sons of Manasseh were the more numerous and they took their inheritance first. And likewise with the princes of the land, he placed him first and traced Joseph's genealogy upon him (Numbers 34:23). But in the section of the spies, he placed Ephraim first, but traced Joseph's genealogy upon Manasseh: \"of the tribe of Joseph, of the tribe of Manasseh\" (Numbers 13:11). And what appears to me by way of aggadah is that on account of the evil report that Joseph brought concerning his brothers (Genesis 37:2), he traced the genealogy upon the one who brings the evil report, or perhaps he divided honor between them both, and it was sufficient for Ephraim to have the honor of his prince."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:02:09.522511509Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}